\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par To see the files contained in a Clic pack you can take the following steps:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab First choose the type of pack (PAC o PCC) you want to see.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Enter the unit and the directory where the pack is to be found.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Click once on its name. The programme will analyse the pack and show a list of all the files contained in it.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par To see more information about any of these files you have to click on its name. In the case of the images (BMP and GIF files) you will be shown a reduced version in the window on
 the right. For texts the content will be shown, and in the case of an activity (PUZ, ASS, SOP, CRW and TXA files) a relation of the variables that determine its working.
\par 
\par You are advised to activate the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Do not explore outside pack directory}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  if this has a very complex structure or if you are accessing activities that are in different directories.
\par 
\par You can also mark the option }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Do not explore pack threadings}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  if you only wish to see the components of a particular pack that forms part of a bigger structure.
\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
\par }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc back.bmp\}}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 INDEX}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057    Back to contents
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\keepn\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \page }{\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain 
