\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 +}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  CF:0030}}$
{\footnote \pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 $ Creating compact Clic packs (PCC)}}}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf2\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Creating compact Clic packs (PCC)
\par }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par To create a compact Clic pack we must start with a normal pack (files with the extension PAC). The compact Clic packs bring all the elements necessary for their
 execution together in one file: activities, texts, images, and other related packs, except for the multimedia files (sounds and videos) and other external files (help, Write, programmes, DLLs, etc.), which have to independently filed so that Windows can 
interpret them.
\par 
\par The steps to follow in creating a compact Clic pack are:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Choose the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Normal Clic pack}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  file }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 (PAC)
\par }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Choose the unit and the directory where the pack is found.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s17\ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab 
Click on the name of the pack to be compacted. If you are dealing with a group of linked packs you should choose the main pack.
\par }\pard\plain \ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab When the process of analysing the pack contents has finished, click on }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Compact }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab In the screen that appears, choose the files that should form part of the compact pack, using the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Exclude}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  and }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Include }{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 buttons. If the pack uses material found in different directories you will also have the possibility of automatically excluding all the files that are not in the main directory.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab 
You can also indicate a specific description for the compact pack, and a different name or directory to the default ones. To avoid problems, you are advised never to change the extension: Clic compact packs must always have the extension PCC.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Once these parameters have been adjusted, click on the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Create compact pack }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par When the programme has finished creating the PCC file, it will propose erasing all the files that have gone into it from the hard disc. It is advisable to accept this option if you want to save space in the hard disc.
\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
\par }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc back.bmp\}}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 INDEX}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057    Back to contents
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\keepn\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \page }{\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain 
