\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 +}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  CF:0040}}$
{\footnote \pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 $ Decompacting PCC packs}}}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf2\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Decompacting PCC packs
\par }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par When Clic uses a compact pack (PCC files) the activity edition functions are deactivated. To carry out any modification, their original format (PAC) will have to be restored.
\par 
\par The steps to follow in returning a compact Clic pack to PAC format are:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \fi-284\li284\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx284\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin284\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Choose the kind of }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Clic Compact pack (PCC) }{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 file.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Choose the unit and the directory where the pack is found.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Click on the name of the pack to be decompacted.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab When the process of analysing its contents has finished, activate the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 Separate }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Choose a unit and directory for extracting the pack contents. The default proposal is that which corresponds to the PCC file.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Choose the files to be decompacted. Initially they will all be marked but it might be of interest to only extract a few of them. You can make multiple choices by 
keeping the [Control] or [Shift] keys pressed while you click on the file names.
\par 
\par \{bmc bola.bmp\}\tab Once the files have been chosen, activate the}{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  Extract }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 button.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par The programme will create the chosen files in the destination directory. This operation will not
 erase the files of the compact pack, but will limit itself to making a copy of them. If all the files of a compact pack have been extracted, we recommend you to erase the PCC files manually in order to free space in the hard disc.
\par 
\par \{bmc linia.bmp\}
\par 
